  "result": "Fixed. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:33` was filtering lines by `l.item.name` when it should have used `l.item.sku`. So `remove('sku-1')` compared the SKU against the name `'Widget'`, nothing matched, and nothing was removed. I changed the comparison to `l.item.sku != sku`.\n\n- **Demo:** `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, so only the Gadget line is left. Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- **Tests:** all 6 pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest`.\n\nNone of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, which is how this got through. I can add a regression test in `tests/` if you'd like.",
